    fleet-ops census: recognize non-GitHub CI providers (FLEET-OPS-CI-001)
    
    The census emitted a P3 "no CI pipeline in the repo — nothing gates a merge" whenever a
    service/library tree lacked a `.github` directory. That is a provider assumption, not a CI
    check: asce and heading both run full pipelines configured in `.gitlab-ci.yml`, so the census
    reported a gap that no work could close, on every tick, for three family aliases (asce,
    HEADING, heading).
    
    The live script (~/.hermes/scripts/fleet_ops_check.py) is outside any repository, so the fix
    ships here as a versioned patch plus the regression arms that prove it:
    
      patches/fleet-ops-ci-markers.patch       diff from sha256 77d1deb2 (pre-fix)
      patches/fleet-ops-ci-markers.test.py     8 arms, target path as argv[1]
    
    Measured:
      pre-fix  (77d1deb2): 3/8 arms pass  -> FAIL on gitlab / circleci / jenkins / azure / live-asce
      post-fix (f393a681): 8/8 arms pass  -> incl. negative control F (a tree with no CI still
                                              reports the gap, so the check is alive, not disabled)
      live census `--json`: check==ci gaps 3 -> 0; P1/P2 flagged families 32 -> 32 (unchanged:
                            this retires phantom P3 noise only, it silences nothing real)
      census rc remains 1, correctly, on the real P1/P2 gaps.
    
    Patch proven both ways: `git apply --check` forward onto the pristine pre-fix copy = 0, and
    `git apply --check --reverse` onto the live patched file = 0 (which is what proves the live
    file equals the patched version).
